{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Or it is made known.</b> Like 'if the matter is made known' — there are many places where אִם and אוֹ serve interchangeably, אִם in place of אוֹ, and likewise ״אוֹ נוֹדַע כִּי שׁוֹר נַגָּח הוּא״ (Exodus 21)." "<b>It is made known to him.</b> When he sinned he thought it was permitted, and afterwards it became known to him that it was forbidden."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:04:59.817500506Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}